b. family environment and alternative care;
c. basic health and welfare;
d. education, leisure time utilization, and cultural activities; ande. special protection.
4. CFC development stages as referred to in paragraph (1), shall include:a. preparation;
b. planning;
c. implementation;
d. monitoring;
e. evaluation; andf. reporting.

